  "body": "Ref https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10432\n\nThis PR integrates the [AsyncContext](https://github.com/tc39/proposal-async-context) proposal into HTML APIs. This PR includes:\n- basic refs to the proposal\n- propagation through APIs that take a callback to signal completion\n- propagation through top-level script execution\n- propagation through APIs that fire events (this is what most of the PR is for). A lot of those APIs actually needed no change, because either they are sync or the event is meant to run in the empty context.\n- propagation to custom element reactions\n\nIt follows the design decisions discussed at past WHATNOT meetings, and written down in https://github.com/tc39/proposal-async-context/blob/master/WEB-INTEGRATION.md / https://github.com/tc39/proposal-async-context/blob/master/web-integration/html__events.md\n\nFor custom element reactions it follows what's currently described in detail at https://github.com/tc39/proposal-async-context/blob/main/web-integration/html__custom-elements.md. That's a new document, but it's the behavior we get by applying the two bullet points we had in `WEB-INTEGRATION.md` about custom elements.\n\nI am maintaining a `gh stack` parallel to this PR with the same changes at https://github.com/nicolo-ribaudo/html/pulls?q=sort%3Acreated-desc%20is%3Apr%20label%3A%22async%20context%22: it was originally there to help myself with tracking the status of what I was doing, but I believe it can also be useful for reviewers to see more detailed context behind why some changes are the way they are (each of those PRs has a semi-detailed list of decisions and things to test in WPT).\n\nThere currently are some open questions:\n- [ ] Whether we should automatically propagate through _queue a microtask_ or not (see https://github.com/nicolo-ribaudo/html/pull/2#issuecomment-6122123355)\n- [ ] Whether we want the `[PropagatesAsyncContextToEvents]` extended attribute defined in https://github.com/whatwg/dom/pull/1451 or not, as at least for HTML the benefits are not super clear. PRs in the stack that use it are at https://github.com/nicolo-ribaudo/html/issues?q=sort%3Acreated-desc%20label%3A%22uses%20PropagatesAsyncContextToEvents%22.\n- [ ] There are a couple XXX notes around `<img>` and media element algorithms with regards to the exact timing that something happens.\n- [ ] The media elements algorithms are in need of a refactor (see https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12502, https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12511, https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2882). I need to help with that and then re-verify that propagation works as expected.\n- [ ] Whether it would be ok implementation-wise to keep the context captured by the `EventSource` constructor alive for as long as that connection is open / being reopened (https://github.com/nicolo-ribaudo/html/pull/11)\n\nCorresponding PRs in other specs that need to land at the same time (they cyclically depend on each other) are https://github.com/whatwg/webidl/pull/1568 and https://github.com/whatwg/dom/pull/1451.\n\n~~I also have a pending WebIDL PR to open to capture the context for rejection in WebIDL-managed promises, so that the `Expose Async Context Mappings on promise rejection events` commit works for them as well as it does for JS-created ones.~~ **UPDATE:** we might make the change in the ECMAScript proposal instead.\n\n---\n\n<!--\nThank you for contributing to the HTML Standard! Please describe the change you are making and complete the checklist below if your change is not editorial.\n\nWhen you submit this PR, and each time you edit this comment (including checking a checkbox through the UI!), PR Preview will run and update it. As such make any edits in one go and only after PR Preview has run.\n\nIf you think your PR is ready to land, please double-check that the build is passing and the checklist is complete before pinging.\n-->\n\n- [ ] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * …\n   * …\n- [ ] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * … <!-- If these tests are tentative, link a PR to make them non-tentative. -->\n- [ ] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: …\n   * Gecko: …\n   * WebKit: …\n   * Deno (only for timers, structured clone, base64 utils, channel messaging, module resolution, web workers, and web storage): …\n   * Node.js (only for timers, structured clone, base64 utils, channel messaging, and module resolution): …\n- [ ] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) & [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues & PRs:\n- [ ] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: …\n- [ ] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use. <!-- If you created this PR from a single commit, Github copied its message. Otherwise, you need to add a commit message yourself. -->\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13063/browsing-the-web.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 30, 2026, 10:21 AM UTC (524df48)\">/browsing-the-web.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13063/86190a4...524df48/browsing-the-web.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 30, 2026, 10:21 AM UTC (524df48)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatp